menu "Example Configuration"

    config EXAMPLE_MQTT_BROKER_URI
        string "MQTT broker URI"
        default "mqtt://raspberrypi.local:1883"
        help
            URI of the MQTT broker to connect to.

            Default assumes a Mosquitto broker running on the Raspberry Pi
            itself (see deploy/mosquitto/), reachable via the mDNS hostname
            Raspberry Pi OS advertises out of the box (avahi-daemon). If mDNS
            doesn't resolve on your network (some hotspots/routers block it),
            replace this with the Pi's LAN IP instead: mqtt://<pi's LAN IP>:1883

            For quick experiments without standing up a broker at all, a
            public test broker also works (not private, don't use for real
            data): mqtt://test.mosquitto.org:1883

    config MPU6050_SDA_GPIO
        int "MPU6050 I2C SDA GPIO"
        default 21
        help
            GPIO connected to the MPU6050's SDA pin.

    config MPU6050_SCL_GPIO
        int "MPU6050 I2C SCL GPIO"
        default 22
        help
            GPIO connected to the MPU6050's SCL pin.

    config MPU6050_INT_GPIO
        int "MPU6050 INT GPIO"
        default 4
        help
            GPIO connected to the MPU6050's INT pin. The sensor pulses this
            line once per internal sample (DATA_RDY, enabled in
            mpu6050_enable_data_ready_interrupt()); app_main.c attaches a
            GPIO ISR here that wakes sample_task, so sampling is driven by
            the sensor's own hardware interrupt rather than a software
            timer.

    config MPU6050_I2C_FREQ_HZ
        int "MPU6050 I2C bus frequency (Hz)"
        default 400000
        help
            I2C clock speed used to talk to the MPU6050.

    config SAMPLE_RATE_HZ
        int "Accelerometer sample rate (Hz)"
        default 500
        help
            Sample rate for the vibration window buffer. This must match
            the rate MPU6050_SMPLRT_DIV_REG is programmed for in
            mpu6050_init() (1kHz / (1 + SMPLRT_DIV) with the DLPF enabled) --
            it's not independently configurable here, since sampling is
            driven by the sensor's own DATA_RDY interrupt at that rate, not
            a separately-timed loop on the ESP32 side. Used for the JSON
            payload's sample_rate_hz field and for picking against Nyquist
            once target mechanical frequencies (motor RPM, belt-pass
            frequency) are known.

    config SAMPLE_WINDOW_SIZE
        int "Samples per published window"
        default 256
        help
            Number of samples buffered per axis before publishing one MQTT
            window as JSON. A power of two is recommended (not required) --
            most FFT implementations are radix-2 and prefer it.

endmenu
